course: dictionary
lesson: 10743
title: Upturned and its two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so read the words around them and choose the meaning that fits. «He sat on an upturned bucket and smoked.» Here upturned means turned upside down, with the open end facing the ground, so the bucket works as a seat.
explain: Upturned can also mean turned or pointing upwards. «She looked up at him with an upturned face» means her face was tipped up towards him. To check your choice, swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The sentence «rain gets into its upturned nose» shows the second meaning. The nose points up to the sky, so the rain falls into it. The clue is the rain and the direction, not the word on its own.
fact: Upturned means turned upside down, or turned and pointing upwards.
fact: An upturned boat is a boat lying upside down.
fact: An upturned bucket can be sat on, as in «a man sitting on an upturned bucket».
fact: An upturned face is a face tipped up to look at something above it.
fact: Phrases to remember: «upturned boat», «upturned bucket», «upturned face», «upturned nose».
exercise: «He was sitting on an upturned bucket by the fire.» What does upturned mean here? | Full of water | *Turned upside down | Cracked and broken | Painted bright red
exercise: «The little girl raised her upturned face to the sun.» What does upturned mean here? | Dirty and muddy | Turned upside down | Hidden behind her hands | *Turned upwards, pointing up
exercise: Which phrase means a boat lying upside down? | fishing net | *upturned boat | sailing boat | boat race
test: «Rain ran into its upturned nose.» In this sentence, upturned means which? | Full of rain | Turned upside down | Covered in fur | *Pointing upwards
test: Ella says upturned always means upside down. Is she right? | Yes, and it also means muddy | *No, it can also mean turned or pointing upwards | No, it means quiet | Yes, it only ever means upside down
exam: Which sentence uses upturned to mean pointing upwards? | «The bucket was full of water.» | *«She smiled with an upturned face.» | «He sat on an upturned bucket.» | «The boat was upturned on the sand.»
